# Site overrides for HOST_ARCH=Linux.
#
# EPICS 3.13.4 is 1990s code that assumes a 32-bit host, and the Solaris tools
# it was built with are 32-bit SPARC. Built x86-64, the dbStatic parser
# silently drops field attributes: dbExpand exits 0 and emits a database with
# no asl() or extra() declarations at all -- 388 lines short of the real one,
# with no warning. So the host tools are built 32-bit.
#
# CC derives from GCC, not ACC: CONFIG_COMMON has CC = $($(ANSI)_$(CMPLR))
# with ANSI=GCC and CMPLR=STRICT, i.e. CC = $(GCC_STRICT) = $(GCC) -ansi
# -pedantic. So GCC and G++ are the override points -- the same ones the
# GEM8.6 tree hardcodes to /usr/local/bin/gcc.
#
# These are wrapper scripts rather than "gcc -m32" because a make
# command-line assignment must be a single word, and because g++ -m32 does
# not search the i686 multilib C++ include directory on Rocky 9 (the wrapper
# adds it).
GCC = gcc32
G++ = g++32
